      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14196466/assets/80bde6a20ceed7c052a87eda6f05c542f6046de7014f6402f5f453b6610f8d42.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14196466/assets/05b25521109f373e2a7718523ce6289b27b37bd185d4fc60f0d052c232f4f8a4.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=-1+x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=-1+x\\,\\}.\n$$",
